# Comparison and Evaluation of Some Economic Models of Digital-Only Journals.

**Authors:** Halliday, Leah, Oppenheim, Charles

## Abstract
Explores economic aspects of digital journal production and delivery using Ithink Analyst, a modeling software package. Three models were developed and simulations were used to monitor the effect of variations in the values of key model elements. Discusses results that show staff costs and overhead are the most substantial costs for scholarly journals. (Author/LRW)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ623504

